 "lead_paragraphs": [
  {
   "label": {
    "en": "CAPITAL RETURNS:",
    "zh": "现金分配："
   },
   "text": {
    "en": "FY12-25 OCF $46.7B less capex $8.1B left **$38.6B FCF**. Dividends **$22.2B (58%)**; buybacks **$19.9B (52%)**; acquisitions **$4.0B**. Dividends plus buybacks exceeded FCF by **$3.5B**, and acquisitions added $4.0B: the difference was borrowed.",
    "zh": "FY12-25 OCF $46.7B 减资本开支 $8.1B，得 **FCF $38.6B**。股息 **$22.2B（58%）**；回购 **$19.9B（52%）**；收购 **$4.0B**。股息加回购超过 FCF **$3.5B**，另有 $4.0B 收购：差额靠举债。"
   }
  },
  {
   "label": {
    "en": "NET SHARES:",
    "zh": "净股数变化："
   },
   "text": {
    "en": "Diluted shares FY11 984M to FY25 811M, **down 17.6%** (about 1.4% a year). FY25: buybacks $1.2B; shares **799.7M** diluted at Q3 2026.",
    "zh": "稀释股数由 FY11 的 984M 降至 FY25 的 811M，**减少 17.6%**（每年约 1.4%）。FY25 回购 $1.2B；2026年Q3 稀释股数 **7.997 亿股**。"
   }
  }
 ],
 "commentary": [
  {
   "headline": {
    "en": "Slow growth, reliable cash.",
    "zh": "增长慢，现金稳。"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Revenue grew only 1.4% a year over 14 years (FX and the 2015 Venezuela exit), but capex never exceeded 4% of sales, so FCF rose from $2.4B to $3.6B and FCF per share 4.6% a year.",
    "zh": "14 年营收年均仅增 1.4%（汇率和 2015 年剥离委内瑞拉），但资本开支从未超过销售的 4%，FCF 由 $2.4B 升至 $3.6B，每股 FCF 年增 4.6%。"
   }
  },
  {
   "headline": {
    "en": "Gross margin is the lever.",
    "zh": "毛利率是关键杠杆。"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Gross margin rebuilt from 57.0% (FY22) to 60.1% (FY25) through pricing and productivity. 2026 brings ~300bp of material cost pressure; Q3 base gross margin still held 60.3%.",
    "zh": "通过提价和降本，毛利率由 FY22 的 57.0% 回升至 FY25 的 60.1%。2026 年面临约 300 个基点的原材料成本压力；Q3 基础毛利率仍保持 60.3%。"
   }
  },
  {
   "headline": {
    "en": "Payouts run ahead of FCF.",
    "zh": "分配超过了 FCF。"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Dividends plus buybacks took 110% of FCF over FY12-25. Book equity is now $365M, so ROE is not meaningful; net debt/EBITDA 1.8x and AA- ratings keep this sustainable. The cost is flexibility: there is little equity cushion if a downturn coincides with a debt maturity.",
    "zh": "FY12-25 股息加回购占 FCF 的 110%。账面权益仅 $365M，ROE 失去意义；净债务/EBITDA 1.8 倍、AA- 评级使这种分配可以持续。代价是灵活性：若经济下行恰逢债务到期，几乎没有权益缓冲。"
   }
  },
  {
   "headline": {
    "en": "Hill's is the growth line, but it cooled.",
    "zh": "Hill's 是增长线，但已降温。"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Hill's grew 15.5% in FY23 and 2.9% in FY25 as private-label volume was exited; margin recovered from 18.8% to 23.1%. Q3 2026 +5.6% with the Fresh launch. Hill's needs mid-single-digit growth for my 2030 revenue path; private-label exit makes that harder to read for a year.",
    "zh": "Hill's 在 FY23 增长 15.5%，FY25 因退出自有品牌代工降至 2.9%；利润率由 18.8% 回升至 23.1%。2026年Q3 在 Fresh 新品带动下 +5.6%。我的 2030 年营收路径需要 Hill's 保持中个位数增长；退出代工后的一年内，这一趋势较难判断。"
   }
  },
  {
   "headline": {
    "en": "Emerging markets carry the profit.",
    "zh": "利润来自新兴市场。"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Latin America is 30% of oral, personal & home care sales at a 29.5% margin, the group's best. That growth comes with currency risk: reported dollars can lag local growth.",
    "zh": "拉丁美洲占口腔、个人与家居护理销售的 30%，利润率 29.5%，为全公司最高。这部分增长伴随汇率风险：美元报表增长可能落后于当地增长。"
   }
  },
  {
   "headline": {
    "en": "The DCF says the stock is fully priced.",
    "zh": "DCF 认为股价已充分反映价值。"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Base $82.56 (WACC 7.5%, g 2.5%, beta 0.6) needs $24.7B sales by 2030 (3.9% a year) at a 22.2% EBIT margin; TV is 82% of EV. At $100.99 that is -18%. Beta decides it: the raw 0.31 gives $111.82. Morningstar ($88, wide moat) also sees the stock as overvalued; its 7.0% WACC alone would lift my value to $94.83.",
    "zh": "基准价值 $82.56（WACC 7.5%，g 2.5%，beta 0.6）要求 2030 年销售 $247 亿（年增 3.9%）、EBIT 利润率 22.2%；终值占 EV 82%。按 $100.99 计为 -18%。结论取决于 beta：用原始 0.31 得 $111.82。Morningstar（$88，宽护城河）同样认为股价偏高；仅把 WACC 换成其 7.0%，我的价值就升至 $94.83。"
   }
  }
 ],
 "footnotes": {
  "en": [
   "FY11-25 from SEC 10-K XBRL (calendar year); Q3 2026 from the Sep 30, 2026 10-Q via the analyst model. Segment and regional data from the 10-K segment table.",
